      "title": "Developers are attached to tools because tools encode trust",
      "url": "https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/07/29/developers-are-attached-to-tools-because-tools-encode-trust/",
      "canonicalUrl": "https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/07/29/developers-are-attached-to-tools-because-tools-encode-trust",
      "summary": "The tools themselves are new and their capabilities are in constant flux. If your kitchen knife kept changing shape, weight, and edge, you\u2019d have to relearn it every time; that\u2019s a hard tool to build trust in. But it also points to a flaw in how you use that tool, the process around it, and the way the tool reinforces the process.",
      "author": "Ryan Donovan",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-29T14:06:38+00:00",
